Bound the short server-Initial frame inspection by the payload end.

picoquic_incoming_server_initial() walks the frames of an unpadded server
Initial starting at the absolute payload offset, but passed the remaining
length to picoquic_skip_frame() as payload_length - byte_index, mixing a
length with an absolute index. A payload shorter than the header offset
wrapped that to a huge size (pointer-overflow UB in picoquic_skip_frame);
a longer one truncated the bound, so a non-ACK frame after a straddling
ACK went unseen and the short Initial was not rejected. The bound is now
ph->offset + ph->payload_length - byte_index.

short_initial_bounds_test covers an ACK-only payload shorter than the
offset, ACK then PING (rejected as PICOQUIC_ERROR_INITIAL_TOO_SHORT), and a
truncated ACK in the node buffer and in an exact-size buffer, asserting the
exact return code and connection error for each.

picoquic_ct now links only picoquic-test, whose interface already carries
the core, log, http and picotls libraries; listing them again made the
link line repeat them. picoquic-test declares the mbedtls libraries its
tests call directly.

Applies to picoquic 55b473e207e436d06ea9a2895cc1fc555d42c81c.

